The interior angle of a regular heptagon is $\frac{5\pi}{7}$ radians, or $\frac{180\cdot 5}{7}$ degrees.  Since $\angle BAC$ is an exterior angle of the heptagon, it is equal to $\frac{2\pi}{7}$ radians, or $\frac{180\cdot 2}{7}$ degrees.

[asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, F;

A = dir(360*3/7+90);
B = dir(360*2/7+90);
C = A + dir(90)*(F - A);
D = C + F - A;
F = dir(360*4/7+90);

draw(A--C--D--F);

label("$A$", A, S);
label("$B$", B, W);
label("$C$", C, SE);
label("$D$", F, S);

draw(A--B--C);

label("$\frac{180\cdot 2}{7}$", (A + B)/2, NW);
[/asy]

Therefore, the degree measure of angle $BAC$ is $\boxed{\frac{360}{7}}$.
